  "body": "Stacked on #2255. The base is `issue/2246-area-preview-fill`. Retarget this PR to `main` before #2255 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/app/src/model/patch_memo.rs`: `model::patches` and `model::patch_rings` memoize `feature::patches` and `feature::patch_rings`. The key is the allocation of the `Arc<Features>`, the same key as `model::resolve_chain` (#2235). A landing makes a new allocation, so it is a new key. The counter is `model::patch_builds`.\n- `State::geo_chips` (welded-face chip label) and `pick::face_origin` read the memo. `face_origin` is used by the chips and by `pick::align_321`.\n- `face_origin` finds the strips of a patch with a binary search in the sorted `Patch::faces`. Before, it did a linear `contains` for each face of the model.\n- `docs/decisions/2247-pick-chip-patches.md`.\n\nThe answers are the same as a fresh grouping. No change to commands, picks, the WCS result, cut geometry or posted G-code.\n\n## Readings (fig8, state c of the #2238 probe, ms for each still frame)\n\n| Piece | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.chips` (release) | 4.68 | see the stack table in #2238 |\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.align_321` (release) | 1.98 | see the stack table in #2238 |\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.chips` (debug) | 12.29 | 0.78 |\n| `ui/properties.op.picks.align_321` (debug) | 11.73 | 0.31 |\n\n## Tests\n\n- `model::patch_memo::tests::a_hit_answers_what_a_fresh_grouping_answers_and_groups_once` (app): a hit equals `feature::patches` and `feature::patch_rings`; a miss is kept; a new allocation groups again.\n- `frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`: the patch counter is 0 on a still frame in states a to e.\n- `frame_cost_caches::pick_chips_group_the_welded_faces_once_and_follow_the_picks` (new): the memo equals a fresh grouping on fig8; still frames group nothing; a new pick gives a new chip list; the undo gives the first chips and the first 3-2-1 answer.\n- `camcraft-app` tests `face_origin`, `plane_align`, `pick_agnostic`, `feature`, `orient_dropdowns`: pass.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: 970 passed, 6 ignored.\n- Clippy `-D warnings`: `camcraft-ui --all-targets` clean; `camcraft-app --lib` and the tests above clean. `camcraft-app --all-targets` does not build on `main`: `crates/app/tests/wire_tool.rs` (not touched here).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other `feature::patches` callers (commands, MCP, heights) do not use the memo. They do not run on each frame.\n- The real window.\n\nChangelog: The operation page with a welded-face pick no longer slows the viewport: the face grouping is computed once for each model.\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2247\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
